1. Create `src/lib/extraction/logger.ts` with console.log wrappers
2. Add timing utilities to measure stage duration
3. Include stage tracking for extraction pipeline
4. Only log in development environment
5. Keep it simple with basic console output

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
class ExtractionLogger {
  private startTime: number;

  logStageStart(stage: string) {
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
      console.log(`[Extraction] ${stage} started`);
      this.startTime = Date.now();
    }
  }

  logStageEnd(stage: string) {
    if (process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') {
      const duration = Date.now() - this.startTime;
      console.log(`[Extraction] ${stage} completed in ${duration}ms`);
    }
  }

  logRetryAttempt(attempt: number, maxAttempts: number) {
    console.log(`[Extraction] Retrying (attempt ${attempt} of ${maxAttempts})...`);
  }
}
```

1. Create `src/lib/extraction/retry-handler.ts` with retry wrapper function
2. Implement exponential backoff: 1s, 2s, 4s between attempts
3. Maximum 3 attempts total
4. Only retry transient errors (FETCH_ERROR, TIMEOUT_ERROR, PARSE_ERROR)
5. Don't retry permanent errors (INVALID_URL)
6. Add cancellation support for user interruption

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
interface RetryConfig {
  maxAttempts: number;
  baseDelay: number;
  retryableErrors: ErrorType[];
}

async function withRetry<T>(
  operation: () => Promise<T>,
  config: RetryConfig,
  logger: ExtractionLogger
): Promise<T> {
  let lastError: ExtractionError;

  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= config.maxAttempts; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await operation();
    } catch (error) {
      lastError = error;

      if (!config.retryableErrors.includes(error.type) || attempt === config.maxAttempts) {
        throw error;
      }

      const delay = config.baseDelay * Math.pow(2, attempt - 1) * 1000;
      logger.logRetryAttempt(attempt + 1, config.maxAttempts);
      await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, delay));
    }
  }

  throw lastError;
}
```

1. Create array of fallback selectors in order of preference
2. Try `#content.content` (current), then `#content`, then `article`
3. Return content from first successful selector
4. Log which selector worked for debugging
5. Modify existing parse logic to use fallback strategy

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
const FALLBACK_SELECTORS = [
  '#content.content',
  '#content', 
  'article',
  '.article-content',
  'main'
];

function parseContentWithFallback(html: string, logger: ExtractionLogger): string {
  const $ = cheerio.load(html);

  for (const selector of FALLBACK_SELECTORS) {
    const content = $(selector).html();
    if (content && content.trim()) {
      logger.logStageEnd(`Parse (using ${selector})`);
      return content;
    }
  }

  throw new ExtractionError({
    type: ErrorType.PARSE_ERROR,
    message: 'No content found with any fallback selector',
    stage: 'parse'
  });
}
```

1. Wrap extraction in retry handler in `src/app/actions/extract-content.ts`
2. Add logging at each extraction stage (fetch, parse, convert)
3. Integrate parsing fallbacks into content extraction
4. Add try-catch wrapper around Markdown conversion with plain text fallback
5. Update UI in `src/app/page.tsx` to show retry attempts
6. Ensure all error types are properly caught and categorized

Pseudo-code:
```typescript
export async function extractContent(url: string): Promise<ExtractionResult> {
  const logger = new ExtractionLogger();
  const retryConfig = {
    maxAttempts: 3,
    baseDelay: 1,
    retryableErrors: [ErrorType.FETCH_ERROR, ErrorType.TIMEOUT_ERROR, ErrorType.PARSE_ERROR]
  };

  return withRetry(async () => {
    // Fetch stage
    logger.logStageStart('fetch');
    const html = await fetchWithTimeout(url);
    logger.logStageEnd('fetch');

    // Parse stage
    logger.logStageStart('parse');
    const content = parseContentWithFallback(html, logger);
    logger.logStageEnd('parse');

    // Convert stage
    logger.logStageStart('convert');
    const markdown = await convertToMarkdownWithFallback(content, logger);
    logger.logStageEnd('convert');

    return { content: markdown, url };
  }, retryConfig, logger);
}

function convertToMarkdownWithFallback(html: string, logger: ExtractionLogger): string {
  try {
    return convertHtmlToMarkdown(html);
  } catch (error) {
    logger.logStageEnd('convert (fallback to plain text)');
    return html.replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ''); // Strip HTML tags
  }
}
```
